\par }\pard\plain \s17\ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\tqc\tx4320\tqr\tx8640\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid2651140 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid3873829         }{\insrsid11689312 
Java is conceived by James Gosling and his coordinators of sun Microsystems. This lang}{\insrsid10698615 uage was initially called the Oak; but was renamed \'93Java\'94 in 1995. Java is similar to the C and C++ languages, but a number of the
 former are eliminated, thus making Java a really simple, secure, reliable, portable and powerful language.}{\insrsid5974129 
\par 
\par }{\insrsid3873829          }{\insrsid5974129 To provide simplicity, Java provides the concept of Package, which is a collection of classes usually done according to some functionality. The Java}{\insrsid5002779  API packages are:
\par 
\par }{\insrsid12407560 Java Lang.}{\fs28\insrsid11689312\charrsid12407560 
\par }{\insrsid12407560 Java Net.}{\fs28\insrsid12407560\charrsid12407560 
\par }{\insrsid12407560 Java util}{\fs28\insrsid12407560\charrsid12407560 
\par }{\insrsid12407560 Java awt}{\fs28\insrsid12407560\charrsid12407560 
\par }{\insrsid12407560 Java applet}{\fs28\insrsid12407560\charrsid12407560 
\par }{\insrsid12407560 Java io}{\fs28\insrsid12407560\charrsid12407560 
\par }{\fs28\insrsid12407560\charrsid11689312 
\par }{\insrsid12407560 Java is two things: a programming language and a platform.}{\insrsid11689312 
\par }{\insrsid12407560 Java as a high-level programming language is preferable because of all the following:
\par Simple
\par Object-oriented
\par Distributed
\par }{\insrsid10248944 Interpreted}{\insrsid12407560 
\par }{\insrsid10248944 Robust
\par Secure
\par Architecture-neutral
\par Portable
\par High-performance
\par }{\insrsid6699070 Multithreaded
\par Dynamic 
\par }{\insrsid2562360 
\par }{\insrsid7612275         }{\insrsid6699070 Java is also unusual in the each Java program is }{\insrsid14251624 both compiled and interpreted.
\par With a compiler, you translate a Java program into an intermediate language called Java bytecodes-the platform-independent codes interpreted by the Java interpreter. With an interpreter, each  Java }{\insrsid13008548 byte code}{\insrsid14251624 
 instruction is parsed and run on the computer. Compilation happens just once; interpretation occurs each time the program is executed. This figure illustrates how this works.  }{\insrsid6699070  }{\insrsid2562360 
\par }{\insrsid2955192     
\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3873829 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid2955192 
