\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3873829 \fs24\lang1033\langfe1033\cgrid\langnp1033\langfenp1033 {\insrsid5977375    }{\insrsid11279756                                    }{\b\insrsid11279756\charrsid3886650 
Fig 4.3 Life cycle of threads}{\b\insrsid5977375\charrsid3886650 
\par }{\b\insrsid11081793 
\par }{\insrsid7496928 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par }{\insrsid11081793\charrsid11081793 There are}{\insrsid11081793  two techniques for providing a run method for a thread;
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f3\insrsid11081793 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls13\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid11081793 {\insrsid11081793 Subclassing Thread And Overriding run
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\f3\insrsid11081793 \loch\af3\dbch\af0\hich\f3 \'b7\tab}Implementing the Runnable Interface
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid11081793 {\insrsid11081793 
\par The following diagram shows the states that a java thread can be in during in its }{\insrsid14763912 life. It also illustrates which method calls cause a transition to another state. This figure is not a complete finite state diagram, but rather an ov
erview of the more interesting and common facts of a thread\rquote s life.  }{\insrsid11081793  
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid3873829 {\insrsid11081793 
\par }{\insrsid14763912 The common states of a thread are as follows-}{\insrsid11081793 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\insrsid14763912 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 a)\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls14\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid6779364 {\insrsid14763912 Newborn- this is the state that thread is in as it is created.
}{\insrsid6779364  However at this point it is not yet scheduled for running. At this point we can do one of the following things with it:
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\insrsid6779364 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1)\tab}}\pard \ql \fi90\li1260\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx900\faauto\ls15\rin0\lin1260\itap0\pararsid7496928 {\insrsid6779364 Schedule it for running using start ( ) method.
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\insrsid6779364 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2)\tab}}\pard \ql \fi630\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls15\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid7496928 {\insrsid6779364 Kill it using stop( )
\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid6779364 {\insrsid6779364 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\insrsid6779364 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 b)\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls14\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid6779364 {\insrsid6779364 Runnable \endash 
 This states means that the thread is ready to run and is waiting for the arability of the processor. This is, it has joined the queue of waiting threads.
\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid7496928 {\insrsid7496928 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\insrsid6779364 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 c)\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls14\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid6779364 {\insrsid6779364 Running - This }{\insrsid10380174 
means that the processor has given its time to thread for execution. The thread continues execution until either.}{\insrsid6779364 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\insrsid15345521 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 1)\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li1800\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx1800\faauto\ls16\rin0\lin1800\itap0\pararsid15345521 {\insrsid15345521 It is suspended using suspend ( ).
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\insrsid15345521 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 2)\tab}It is sent to dormant state using sleep ( ).
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\insrsid15345521 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 3)\tab} It is told to wait the occurrence of some event.
\par }\pard \ql \li1440\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin1440\itap0\pararsid7496928 {\insrsid7496928 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\insrsid15345521 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 d)\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls14\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid15345521 {\insrsid15345521 
Blocked- A thread is said to be blocked when it is prevented from entering into the runnable state and subsequently the running state.
\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid7496928 {\insrsid7496928 
\par {\listtext\pard\plain\insrsid15345521 \hich\af0\dbch\af0\loch\f0 e)\tab}}\pard \ql \fi-360\li720\ri0\nowidctlpar\jclisttab\tx720\faauto\ls14\rin0\lin720\itap0\pararsid15345521 {\insrsid15345521 Dead \endash 
 This is the state that the thread is in after it has completed execution of it\rquote s run ( ) method.
\par }\pard \ql \li360\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin360\itap0\pararsid15345521 {\insrsid15345521 
\par }{\b\fs28\insrsid2644192\charrsid10238224 J}{\b\i\fs28\insrsid2644192\charrsid7371392 ava Developer\rquote s Kit
\par }{\insrsid2644192 
\par Java is actually more than a computer language; it\rquote s also a programming environment that}{\insrsid15345521\charrsid2644192  }{\insrsid2644192 
includes a complete set of programming tools. These tools include a compiler, an interpreter, a debugger, a }{\insrsid941647 dissembler}{\insrsid2644192 , a profiler, and more. To c
reate a Java program, you first use a text editor to create the source-code file. You write the source code, of course, in the Java language. After completing }{\insrsid12327829 
the source code, which is always saved with a Java file extension, you compile the program into i
ts byte-code format, the file for which has the .class file extension. It is the .class file that the interpreter lodes and execute. Because the byte-code files are fully portable between operating system, they can be executed on any system that has a Jav
a interpreter.
\par 
\par }{\insrsid9270401 
\par 
\par }{\insrsid5178914 
\par }{\insrsid12327829 After compiling and running a Java program, you may discover that the source code needs }{\insrsid14429240 
modification. The Java debugger can help you find your errors, whereas the Java profiler provides handy information about your program. If you run into a compiled Java program that you\rquote d like to see in source-code form, the Java }{\insrsid941647 
dissembler}{\insrsid14429240  will do the translation for you. Java also includes a program that creates the file you need to take advantage of native methods (function written in another language, such as C++). There\rquote 
s even a program that can create HTML documents from Java }{\insrsid3878741 sources-code files, although all the development tools are DOS applications-that is, they don\rquote 
t run under windows-they provide a complete environment for creating and managing Java project.    }{\insrsid14429240     }{\insrsid12327829     }{\insrsid2644192      }{\insrsid15345521\charrsid2644192   
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid15345521 {\insrsid15345521 
\par }{\b\fs32\insrsid9396917\charrsid10238224 A}{\b\insrsid9396917\charrsid10238224 bstract}{\b\fs28\insrsid9396917\charrsid941647  }{\b\fs32\insrsid9396917\charrsid10238224 W}{\b\insrsid9396917\charrsid10238224 indowing}{
\b\fs28\insrsid9396917\charrsid941647  }{\b\fs32\insrsid9396917\charrsid10238224 T}{\b\insrsid9396917\charrsid10238224 oolkit}{\b\fs28\insrsid15345521 
\par }{\b\fs28\insrsid7371392\charrsid941647 
\par }{\b\i\fs28\insrsid9396917\charrsid7371392 Introduction to the }{\b\fs28\insrsid9396917\charrsid8343633 AWT}{\b\i\fs28\insrsid9396917\charrsid7371392 
\par }{\b\insrsid9396917 
\par }{\insrsid9396917 The classes and interface of the Abstract Windowing Toolkit (AWT) are used to develop stand-alone application and to implement the}{\insrsid9777103 
 GUI controls used by applets. These classes support all aspects of GUI development, including event handling.
\par 
\par The components and container classes are two of the most important classes in the Java .awt package. The component class provides a common super
 class for all classes that implement GUI controls. The container class is subclass of the components class and can contain other AWT components. It is well worth your while }{\insrsid2508787 
to familiarize yourself with the API description of these two classes.}{\insrsid15345521 
\par }{\insrsid2508787 
\par The window
 class is a substance of the container class that provides a common set of methods for implementing windows. The window class has two subclasses, Frame and Dialog that are used to create window objects. The Frame class is used to create a main application
 window, and the Dialog class is used to implement dialog boxes.  
\par }{\insrsid15345521 
\par }{\insrsid9270401 
